  "codexOpeningTitle": "The roads of Lothringen",
  "@codexOpeningTitle": {
    "description": "Codex world-reference prose: codexOpeningTitle. Preserve canonical names and meaning; do not invent lore. Instructions use tu in French."
  },
  "codexOpening": "Théodonis stands behind old walls, surrounded by farmland and forests. The city has survived wars, raids and disease, and its apparent stability rests on institutions that have weathered many crises.\n\nLong ago, Éloïse founded La Main to confront a hidden threat. After her disappearance, the order continued its work in secret. More recently, an incident at the Villa Twinsen left questions unanswered.\n\nOn the roads of Lothringen, Neyla leads a traveling company of performers. They bring shows to the communities they visit and offer help along the way. Their journey now leads toward Théodonis.",
  "@codexOpening": {
    "description": "Codex world-reference prose: codexOpening. Preserve canonical names and meaning; do not invent lore. Instructions use tu in French."
  },
  "codexGrojibLore": "Grojib closes the distance without hesitation. A traveler who holds their ground after the first blow may find another strike already on its way.",
  "@codexGrojibLore": {
    "description": "Codex world-reference prose: codexGrojibLore. Preserve canonical names and meaning; do not invent lore. Instructions use tu in French."
  },
  "codexHashashLore": "Hashash fights from the uncertainty of the forest, appearing where attention has already moved on. In these woods, an apparently empty path is no promise of safe passage.",
  "@codexHashashLore": {
    "description": "Codex world-reference prose: codexHashashLore. Preserve canonical names and meaning; do not invent lore. Instructions use tu in French."
  },
  "codexDerfLore": "Derf’s outward form conceals a transformation that turns a distant spellcaster into a pursuing, tentacled threat.",
  "@codexDerfLore": {
    "description": "Codex world-reference prose: codexDerfLore. Preserve canonical names and meaning; do not invent lore. Instructions use tu in French."
  },
  "codexUnocoLore": "The Unoco demons encountered over the forest carry the threat above the paths, where walls and broken ground offer little protection from a spell cast out of the air.",
  "@codexUnocoLore": {
    "description": "Codex world-reference prose: codexUnocoLore. Preserve canonical names and meaning; do not invent lore. Instructions use tu in French."
  },
  "codexBringerLore": "The Bringer of Death bars the way through a clearing claimed by the darkness. Its scythe and rising pillars leave little room for hesitation. Defeating this guardian opens a way deeper into the forest.",
  "@codexBringerLore": {
    "description": "Codex world-reference prose: codexBringerLore. Preserve canonical names and meaning; do not invent lore. Instructions use tu in French."
  },
  "codexGoddessLore": "The name Voidborn Goddess records the terror of the encounter, not proof of divinity. This presence turns the clearing itself into a threat. What brought it into the forest remains unknown.",
  "@codexGoddessLore": {
    "description": "Codex world-reference prose: codexGoddessLore. Preserve canonical names and meaning; do not invent lore. Instructions use tu in French."
  },
  "codexShoggothLore": "Shoggoth is encountered among the deeper horrors guarding the route. Smaller creatures accompany its assaults, making the fight feel less like a duel than a struggle to keep a patch of ground. Its distant origin remains unrecorded.",
  "@codexShoggothLore": {
    "description": "Codex world-reference prose: codexShoggothLore. Preserve canonical names and meaning; do not invent lore. Instructions use tu in French."
  },
  "codexVoidcallerLore": "The Voidcaller’s presence is marked by beams, erupting claws and summoned tentacles. Its title describes what travelers have witnessed, while the nature of what answers its call remains uncertain.",
  "@codexVoidcallerLore": {
    "description": "Codex world-reference prose: codexVoidcallerLore. Preserve canonical names and meaning; do not invent lore. Instructions use tu in French."
  },
  "codexShoggothMinionLore": "These smaller creatures enter the fight at Shoggoth’s summons. They are part of the same immediate threat, pressing an opponent while the larger creature prepares its next assault. Their appearance is a warning that the ground around Shoggoth will not stay clear.",
  "@codexShoggothMinionLore": {
    "description": "Codex world-reference prose: codexShoggothMinionLore. Preserve canonical names and meaning; do not invent lore. Instructions use tu in French."
  },
  "codexVoidTentacleLore": "A tentacle called into the arena is a local expression of the Voidcaller’s reach. It makes dangerous ground out of a place that was open a moment before. Destroying it removes that threat, but leaves the power calling it forth to be confronted.",
  "@codexVoidTentacleLore": {
    "description": "Codex world-reference prose: codexVoidTentacleLore. Preserve canonical names and meaning; do not invent lore. Instructions use tu in French."
  },
  "codexGrojibTactics": "A ground pursuer with a follow-up melee strike that can stun on hit. Leave room for the second swing.",
  "@codexGrojibTactics": {
    "description": "Codex world-reference prose: codexGrojibTactics. Preserve canonical names and meaning; do not invent lore. Instructions use tu in French."
  },
  "codexHashashTactics": "A mobile assassin with a teleporting ambush. Watch for its return before committing.",
  "@codexHashashTactics": {
    "description": "Codex world-reference prose: codexHashashTactics. Preserve canonical names and meaning; do not invent lore. Instructions use tu in French."
  },
  "codexDerfTactics": "Transforms from a caster into a melee pursuer. Its extended tentacle gives the strike unusual reach.",
  "@codexDerfTactics": {
    "description": "Codex world-reference prose: codexDerfTactics. Preserve canonical names and meaning; do not invent lore. Instructions use tu in French."
  },
  "codexUnocoTactics": "A flying caster that can also strike at close range. Keep moving while its projectile is aimed.",
  "@codexUnocoTactics": {
    "description": "Codex world-reference prose: codexUnocoTactics. Preserve canonical names and meaning; do not invent lore. Instructions use tu in French."
  },
  "codexBringerTactics": "A scythe fighter with dark pillars. Read the wind-up and move clear of the marked ground.",
  "@codexBringerTactics": {
    "description": "Codex world-reference prose: codexBringerTactics. Preserve canonical names and meaning; do not invent lore. Instructions use tu in French."
  },
  "codexGoddessTactics": "Combines claw attacks, dark orbs and ground eruptions. Reposition when the arena is threatened.",
  "@codexGoddessTactics": {
    "description": "Codex world-reference prose: codexGoddessTactics. Preserve canonical names and meaning; do not invent lore. Instructions use tu in French."
  },
  "codexShoggothTactics": "Uses tentacles, dark orbs and summoned creatures. Manage the smaller threats while watching the boss.",
  "@codexShoggothTactics": {
    "description": "Codex world-reference prose: codexShoggothTactics. Preserve canonical names and meaning; do not invent lore. Instructions use tu in French."
  },
  "codexVoidcallerTactics": "Uses vertical and diagonal beams, fire claws and tentacle summons. Keep a route out of overlapping attacks.",
  "@codexVoidcallerTactics": {
    "description": "Codex world-reference prose: codexVoidcallerTactics. Preserve canonical names and meaning; do not invent lore. Instructions use tu in French."
  },
  "codexShoggothMinionTactics": "A small ground attacker summoned by Shoggoth. Avoid being crowded while the boss attacks.",
  "@codexShoggothMinionTactics": {
    "description": "Codex world-reference prose: codexShoggothMinionTactics. Preserve canonical names and meaning; do not invent lore. Instructions use tu in French."
  },
  "codexVoidTentacleTactics": "A summoned melee threat. Move beyond its lash before turning to attack it.",
  "@codexVoidTentacleTactics": {
    "description": "Codex world-reference prose: codexVoidTentacleTactics. Preserve canonical names and meaning; do not invent lore. Instructions use tu in French."
  },
  "codexForestLore": "Val Outpost stands beside the road through the Long-Eared Owls’ Forest. Its soldiers patrol the wooded route, train for the forest’s hazards, and carry warnings of danger back to Théodonis. Travelers can rest under their guard before continuing their journey.",
  "@codexForestLore": {
    "description": "Codex world-reference prose: codexForestLore. Preserve canonical names and meaning; do not invent lore. Instructions use tu in French."
  },
  "codexFieldLore": "Léonards’ farm is the largest agricultural estate around Théodonis. A powerful family oversees its fields and harvests.",
  "@codexFieldLore": {
    "description": "Codex world-reference prose: codexFieldLore. Preserve canonical names and meaning; do not invent lore. Instructions use tu in French."
  },
